-- ============================================================================
-- DR5 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Geomechanics, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: wellbore stability at a point. Drilling a hole
-- CONCENTRATES the stress the removed rock was carrying, and for a circular
-- hole the far-field difference is amplified by exactly four at the wall. Two
-- rotations take the far field into the borehole frame, and the shear terms
-- they produce are the entire difference between the vertical problem and the
-- deviated one. The mud IS the radial stress: it lowers the hoop stress and
-- raises the radial one at once, closing the Mohr-Coulomb gap at one plus q
-- per unit of pressure while the fracture margin worsens at only one per unit,
-- which is why the window is asymmetric.
--
-- TWO CRITERIA AND THEIR HONEST LABELS. Collapse is Mohr-Coulomb over a one
-- degree theta sweep at ZERO breakout width, which is the pressure at which a
-- breakout would just BEGIN rather than the pressure at which the hole becomes
-- unusable; real holes tolerate 30 to 60 degrees routinely. Fracture
-- initiation is a hoop-tension criterion on the intact wall, which is NOT a
-- leak-off prediction, NOT a propagation pressure and NOT a lost circulation
-- pressure, and it is an over-estimate for losses wherever natural fractures
-- exist. The lower bound is the LARGER of the collapse pressure and the pore
-- pressure, and which one wins changes with depth: at 1000 m collapse binds at
-- 1374.158459503409 kg/m3 against a pore pressure gradient of 1030, and at
-- 2500 m the pore pressure binds by a wide margin.
--
-- THE STRONGEST CHECK IN THE COURSE. The vertical fixture's collapse and
-- fracture pressures both have closed forms, and the engine reproduces them
-- EXACTLY rather than nearly. m04 derives both in two lines. A golden from
-- another implementation says two programs agree; a closed form says the
-- program agrees with the mathematics.
--
-- A NUMERICAL FINDING WORTH RECORDING. The worst Mohr-Coulomb margin is NOT
-- monotone in the well pressure, because at high pressure the RADIAL stress
-- becomes the largest wall stress and the gap opens again. A naive bisection
-- would converge on the second crossing and report a collapse pressure above
-- the fracture pressure, which is an inverted window and a spectacular wrong
-- answer from a subtle numerical assumption. The engine scans 400 steps for
-- the FIRST crossing before bisecting, and the oracle mirrors the spec.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

